<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">DP World</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2005</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">DP World is a multinational port and logistics company based in Dubai, United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>, formed in 2005 by merging the Dubai Ports Authority and Dubai Ports International. It operates container terminals on six continents, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebel-ali">Jebel Ali</a> in Dubai. In 2016 it signed a 30-year concession to develop and run the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbera">Berbera</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dp-world.jpg" alt="DP World" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DP World · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DP_World_2021_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
